    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d316">

                <pb facs="0518" n="448" sameAs="frus:frus1867p2/pg448"/>

                <head>Mr. Otterbourg to Mr.
                        Seward</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 6.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">City of Mexico,</hi>
                        </placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1867-08-20"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >August</hi> 20, 1867</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Pursuant to instructions from the State
                    Department under date July 12th, 1867, received here on the 15th August, I
                    immediately addressed a note (enclosure No. 1) to Mr. Lerdo de Tejada, minister
                    for foreign affairs, to which enclosure No. 2 is a reply.</p>
                <p>Enclosure No. 3 is a copy of the customary address to the President of the
                    Mexican republic on the presentation of my credentials. The spirit therein
                    displayed as a just interpretation of our policy towards Mexico will, I hope,
                    meet the approval of the President and of the department.</p>
                <p>No. 4 is a copy of the reply thereto of President Juarez.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, very respectfully, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>MARCUS OTTERBOURG.</signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of State, Washington, D C.</hi></p>
                </postscript>





